5. USAGE DATA

   The Software can send anonymous usage counts: the country, the version in
   use and which set of features is enabled, how many targets are managed and
   of which kind, the Business Central version of those targets shortened to
   major and minor, and which commands are launched, how many times and on
   what kind of target. No name of a server, service instance, tenant,
   database, account, company or extension is ever sent, no path, no error
   message text, no name this copy is registered to and no fingerprint it is
   tied to, and no content of the systems you administer is read for this
   purpose.

   The counts are received by Microsoft Azure Application Insights and cannot be
   traced back to you. Sending can be switched off at any time, in Settings,
   under "Privacy". The complete notice is reproduced in the application, on
   that same page, and states what is sent, what never is, where it waits and
   for how long it is kept.

